# Owned security-only package evidence

`review.py` independently reconciles all original ownership/Root-map bounds,
the real Cargo archive, both full library catalogs and external registry callers,
and complete policy under both package identities. No archived code is executed.
`packet.py` retains first R1–R4 refusals as well as R5, producers, exact sources,
the package archive and whole checked RustSec snapshot. Build caches and private
Cargo homes are excluded. `verify DIGEST` checks whole bytes and independent
semantics; `restore DIGEST target/NEW` exports only the exact package source,
refuses existing/outside destinations, and never builds or runs it.

`test_result.py` includes coherently rehashed mutation controls. Local registry
success cannot authorize actual publication, Root adoption, MTU/resource/CPU/RSS,
upstream integration-target runtime or release admission. Preserve all original
checks, first refusals, deadlines and thresholds.
